# UI UX Pro Max Router

Canon: `DESIGN.md` tokens > project CSS > skill DB suggestions.
Skill: `/ui-ux-pro-max` → `.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md`
Spec: `documents/superpowers/specs/2026-06-13-ui-ux-pro-max-integration.md`

## Trigger

UI/UX design, layout, styling, component work, or visual refresh on matched paths.
Read `DESIGN.md` first; run skill `--design-system` before implementing.

## Workflow

1. Read `DESIGN.md` (colors, typography, spacing).
2. Design system CLI:
   ```bash
   python .cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py "<feature> dark OLED factory dashboard" --design-system --stack html-tailwind -p "shapez2 Factory Planner"
   ```
3. Map skill output to project tokens — **never replace** canon hex/fonts.
4. Tailwind in templates or `@layer components` in `assets/css/input.css`.
5. Verify: `npm run build:css`; visible UI → `/playwright` when practical.

## Project tokens (override skill defaults)

| Role | Value |
|------|-------|
| primary / bg | `#020617` |
| surface | `#0F172A` |
| accent | `#22D3EE`, `#06B6D4` |
| success | `#34D399` |
| Font | `Google Sans Code`; mono `Fira Code` |

## Rules

- Dark OLED factory-console only — skip light-only skill styles.
- No Glassmorphism/Neumorphism unless dark-adapted and token-aligned.
- Keep `lab-*` compatible; no business logic in templates/CSS.
- Skill vs `DESIGN.md` conflict → report; do not silently override canon.

Prompt: `.cursor/prompts/ui-design.md`. Refs: `web-interface.mdc`, `frontend/AGENTS.md`.
